<%# crosswire:contract v1 %>
<%#
  Deliberately dumb — every class/state decision lives in Crosswire::UI::Select, so
  this file is safe to restyle, shadow, or eject. See docs/DECISIONS.md D6.

  `content` is the caller's own <option>/<optgroup> markup — crosswire generates
  none of its own (Rule 0; see the presenter's docstring). The server-rendered
  `selected` attribute on one of those options is the Morph: Server-owned value —
  see the presenter's docstring and test/js/select.browser.test.js.

  Locals:
    select   Crosswire::UI::Select
    content  String or nil — already-captured <option> markup
%>
<%= content_tag(:select, select.attrs) { content } %>
